---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms & Privacy"
  description="Terms of use and privacy information for the Pervasive Capital website."
>
  <section class="page-hero legal-hero">
    <div class="shell content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use &amp; Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated: 29 July 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="shell legal-grid">
      <aside>
        <nav aria-label="Legal page sections">
          <a href="#terms">Terms of Use</a>
          <a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
          <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        </nav>
        <p>
          This general website policy should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before
          publication.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div class="legal-copy">
        <article id="terms">
          <p class="eyebrow">Part one</p>
          <h2>Terms of Use</h2>

          <h3>1. About this website</h3>
          <p>
            This website is operated for Pervasive Capital Investments Pte. Ltd.
            (“Pervasive Capital”, “we”, “us”, or “our”). By accessing or using this website,
            you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do not agree, please do not use the website.
          </p>

          <h3>2. Information only</h3>
          <p>
            The content on this website is provided for general corporate and informational
            purposes only. It does not constitute, and should not be relied on as, financial,
            investment, legal, tax, technical, or other professional advice. Nothing on this
            website is an offer, invitation, recommendation, or solicitation to buy or sell
            any security, financial instrument, product, or service.
          </p>

          <h3>3. Forward-looking information</h3>
          <p>
            This website may describe proposed projects, strategies, objectives, market
            opportunities, or other forward-looking matters. Such statements involve assumptions,
            risks, and uncertainties. Actual activities and results may differ materially, and
            we do not undertake to update forward-looking information except where required by law.
          </p>

          <h3>4. Accuracy and availability</h3>
          <p>
            We aim to keep the website useful and accurate but do not warrant that its content is
            complete, current, error-free, or suitable for a particular purpose. We may change,
            suspend, or withdraw any part of the website without notice.
          </p>

          <h3>5. Intellectual property</h3>
          <p>
            Unless otherwise stated, the website’s text, design, graphics, and other original
            materials are owned by or licensed to Pervasive Capital. You may view and make
            reasonable copies for personal, non-commercial reference. No other reproduction,
            modification, distribution, or commercial use is permitted without prior written
            consent or an applicable legal right.
          </p>

          <h3>6. External links</h3>
          <p>
            Links to third-party websites are provided for convenience. We do not control and
            are not responsible for their content, availability, security, or privacy practices.
            A link does not imply endorsement.
          </p>

          <h3>7. Limitation of liability</h3>
          <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by law, Pervasive Capital and its officers, employees,
            and representatives exclude liability for loss or damage arising from access to,
            reliance on, or inability to use this website, including indirect or consequential
            loss. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
          </p>

          <h3>8. Governing law</h3>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of Singapore. You agree to submit disputes
            relating to this website to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of the Singapore courts.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="privacy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Part two</p>
          <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

          <h3>1. Information this website collects</h3>
          <p>
            This is a static website. We do not use analytics, advertising trackers, user accounts,
            or non-essential cookies, and the website does not directly receive or store the
            information entered into the contact form.
          </p>

          <h3>2. Contact enquiries</h3>
          <p>
            The contact form prepares an email in your chosen email application. If you send that
            email, we receive the information you include, such as your name, email address,
            organisation, message, and any later correspondence. Your email provider and ours may
            process that information under their own terms and privacy policies.
          </p>

          <h3>3. How we use correspondence</h3>
          <p>
            We may use enquiry information to respond to you, assess a proposed relationship or
            opportunity, maintain business records, protect our legitimate interests, and comply
            with legal obligations. We do not sell contact information.
          </p>

          <h3>4. Disclosure and retention</h3>
          <p>
            We may share correspondence with personnel, professional advisers, service providers,
            affiliates, or authorities where reasonably necessary for the purposes above or
            required by law. We retain it only for as long as reasonably needed for those purposes.
          </p>

          <h3>5. Security and international processing</h3>
          <p>
            We take reasonable steps to protect information we receive, but no email or electronic
            system is completely secure. Depending on the services used to transmit and manage
            correspondence, information may be processed outside Singapore.
          </p>

          <h3>6. Your choices</h3>
          <p>
            You may contact us to ask about personal information you have sent, request a correction,
            or raise a privacy concern. Applicable rights and exceptions depend on the relevant law
            and circumstances.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="contact">
          <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about these terms or our handling of correspondence, email
            <a href="mailto:contact@pervasive-capital.com">contact@pervasive-capital.com</a>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .legal-hero {
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .legal-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 5.4rem);
  }

  .legal-section {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0;
  }

  .legal-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 48rem);
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 4rem;
  }

  aside {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);
    align-self: start;
  }

  aside nav {
    display: grid;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  aside nav a {
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  aside nav a:hover {
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  aside p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
  }

  article {
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);
  }

  article + article {
    margin-top: 6rem;
    padding-top: 5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  article h2 {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    color: var(--navy);
  }

  article h3 {
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.65rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.04rem;
  }

  article p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  article a {
    color: var(--teal);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .legal-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    aside {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
